AIM
To develop a responsive web layout using CSS Flexbox and Grid that adjusts automatically to different screen sizes.

procedure:

 Responsive Web Design – Flexbox and Grid
1. Create an HTML file.
2. Design a header, navigation menu and content cards.
3. Apply CSS Flexbox and Grid properties.
4. Add media queries for tablet and mobile screens.
5. Save as 2.html and resize the browser to test responsiveness.



PROGRAM
Save the following code as 2.html and open it in a browser. Resize the browser window to check the layout.

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Responsive Layout</title>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            background-color: #f2f2f2;
            margin: 0;
        }
        header {
            background-color: #333;
            color: white;
            padding: 20px;
            display: flex;
            justify-content: space-between;
            align-items: center;
        }
        nav {
            display: flex;
            gap: 20px;
        }
        nav a {
            color: white;
            text-decoration: none;
        }
        .container {
            width: 90%;
            margin: 30px auto;
            display: grid;
            grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
            gap: 20px;
        }
        .card {
            background-color: white;
            padding: 25px;
            text-align: center;
            border-radius: 8px;
        }
        @media (max-width: 768px) {
            .container {
                grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
            }
            header {
                flex-direction: column;
                gap: 15px;
            }
        }
        @media (max-width: 480px) {
            .container {
                grid-template-columns: 1fr;
            }
            nav {
                flex-direction: column;
                text-align: center;
            }
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <header>
        <h1>Responsive Web Design</h1>
        <nav>
            <a href="#">Home</a>
            <a href="#">About</a>
            <a href="#">Services</a>
            <a href="#">Contact</a>
        </nav>
    </header>

    <main class="container">
        <div class="card"><h2>HTML</h2><p>Creates webpage structure.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h2>CSS</h2><p>Styles the webpage.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h2>Flexbox</h2><p>Arranges items in one direction.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h2>Grid</h2><p>Arranges items in rows and columns.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h2>Responsive Design</h2><p>Adapts to screen sizes.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h2>Web Development</h2><p>Builds websites.</p></div>
    </main>
</body>
</html>

OUTPUT
The webpage displays a header, navigation menu and six content cards.
- Desktop: cards appear in three columns.
- Tablet: cards appear in two columns.
- Mobile: cards appear in one column.

RESULT
Thus, a responsive web layout was successfully developed using CSS Flexbox, Grid and media queries.
